blocks.markdown:
Tags of every experience in the current activation chain: the leaf, its required ancestry, and whichever optional dependencies were present.

This is the query half of the optional-dependency contract. A dependent that declared an optional want copes with absence by asking here and branching — no asset reference to content that may not exist.

@return Tags of the live chain; filled when activation starts, empty when nothing is set.

types.description:
Gantry ships this and nothing derived from it. AddComponents, AddAbilities, AddWidgets and their kin are all game-shaped, and a framework that ships them is a framework built for one game.

The value here is the async contract the engine does not provide. Override BeginActivation instead of OnGameFeatureActivating, and call FinishActivation when the work is genuinely done — which may be several frames later: void UMyAction::BeginActivation(const FGameFeatureActivatingContext& Context) { Manager->RequestAsyncLoad(Paths, FStreamableDelegate::CreateUObject( this, &UMyAction::HandleLoaded)); } void UMyAction::HandleLoaded() { FinishActivation(); }

A synchronous action overrides nothing extra; the default BeginActivation finishes at once. This mirrors UGantryExperienceStage's BeginStage/FinishStage, so there is one idiom for "override Begin, call Finish, async is free" across the whole plugin.
